[{:adr/consequences "{:operator-benefit \"auditable forkable operations-coordination platform, no closed back-office SaaS lock-in\", :structural-guarantee \"actor cannot finalize refund/replacement/chargeback/vendor-registration-revocation or a counterfeit-authenticity determination on its own initiative\", :maturity-summary-delta {:implemented \"+1\"}, :extension-pattern \"add new op to closed allowlist with its own HARD checks + tests, same independent-governor-reverifies-against-actor-own-records pattern\"}", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2700004771", :adr/context "{:registry-entry {:name-before-truncated \"Retail sale of clothing, footwear and leather articles in s...\", :business-id-before \"cloud-itonami-G4771\", :name-after \"Retail sale of clothing, footwear and leather articles in specialized stores\", :maturity-before :spec, :repo-before \"https://github.com/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-G4771\", :maturity-after :implemented, :id \"4771\", :business-id-after \"cloud-itonami-isic-4771\", :repo-after \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4771\"}, :fresh-scaffold? true, :pre-existing-repo-checks [{:repo \"gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-G4771\", :status 404} {:repo \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4771\", :status 404, :note \"checked before any work began\"}], :truncation-bug {:known-issue? true, :rate-estimate \"~10% pre-existing seed-data bug\", :precedent-adr \"ADR-2695004753\"}, :group-entry-untouched {:id \"477\", :name \"Retail sale of other goods in specialized stores\", :superseded-by [\"4772\" \"4774\"]}, :distinct-from [{:id \"4751\", :reason \"textile/fabric/yardage retail, not finished garments\"} {:id \"4719\", :reason \"non-specialized general merchandise retail\"}]}", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/wave 2, :adr/body "# ADR-2700004771: cloud-itonami ISIC 4771 clothing/footwear/leather retail coverage\n\n- Status: accepted\n- Date: 2026-07-16\n- Wave: 2 (coordination/logistics/trade, ADR-2607121000)\n\n## Context\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry`'s `registry.edn` carries an ISIC Rev.5 class-level\nentry `{:id \"4771\" ...}` -- \"Retail sale of clothing, footwear and\nleather articles in specialized stores\" -- at `:maturity :spec` with a\nstale placeholder `:repo`/`:business-id`\n(`https://github.com/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-G4771` /\n`cloud-itonami-G4771`). Independently confirmed via `gh api` that\nneither that stale placeholder repo nor the real target\n(`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4771`) existed before this work --\nthis is a fresh scaffold, not an extension of prior work.\n\nThe live registry `:name` string for this entry was truncated with a\nliteral `\"...\"` (a known ~10% pre-existing seed-data bug in this\nregistry, already observed and fixed in several sibling entries, e.g.\nISIC 4753's own de-truncation in ADR-2695004753): `\"Retail sale of\nclothing, footwear and leather articles in s...\"`. This ADR's own\nregistry edit de-truncates it to the full ISIC class name as part of the\nsame exact-block edit.\n\nA separate, coarser-granularity `{:id \"477\" ...}` 3-digit group entry\n(`\"Retail sale of other goods in specialized stores\"`,\n`:superseded-by [\"4772\" \"4774\"]`) already exists in the registry as a\ndistinct, redundant registry artifact and is deliberately left untouched\nby this work.\n\nISIC 4771 is distinct from sibling apparel/textile-adjacent retail\nclasses already implemented in this fleet: ISIC 4751 (Retail sale of\ntextiles in specialized stores -- fabric/notions/yardage, not finished\ngarments) and ISIC 4719 (Other retail sale in non-specialized stores --\ngeneral merchandise, not a specialized clothing/footwear/leather\nstorefront).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4771` as a fresh OSS actor\nrepository mirroring the verified `cloud-itonami-isic-4751` module shape\nmodule-for-module (`apparelops.*` namespace in place of `textileops.*`):\n\n- **ApparelRetailAdvisor ⊣ ApparelRetailGovernor** -- a clothing/\n  footwear/leather-articles specialized-store retail\n  OPERATIONS-COORDINATION actor, built on `kotoba-lang/langgraph`\n  (portable `.cljc`, langgraph-clj StateGraph, `intake -> advise ->\n  govern -> decide -> commit | hold | request-approval`, real\n  `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` human-in-the-loop, not a stub).\n- Closed four-op proposal allowlist, all `:effect :propose`:\n  `:log-sales-record` (inventory/sale/return/alteration transaction\n  logging), `:schedule-staffing-operation` (floor-staff/fitting-room\n  scheduling), `:coordinate-supply-order` (apparel/footwear/leather-\n  goods inventory-procurement coordination), `:flag-quality-concern`\n  (defective-garment/mis-sized/mislabeled/suspected-counterfeit concern\n  flagging).\n- Four HARD, permanent, un-overridable-by-human-approval governor\n  checks: (1) **store-unverified** -- the target store's business\n  registration must exist AND be independently `:registered?`/\n  `:verified?` in the store before any proposal for it may commit or\n  even escalate; (2) **vendor-unverified** -- for\n  `:coordinate-supply-order` only, the proposal's own drafted\n  `:vendor-id` must resolve to an independently registered/verified\n  vendor record, a supply-chain counterparty-verification gate mirroring\n  ISIC 4751/4719's own; (3) **effect-not-propose** -- any `:effect`\n  other than `:propose` is a hard block; (4) **scope-exclusion** (folds\n  in op-not-allowed) -- permanently blocks any proposal touching\n  directly finalizing a quality-dispute resolution (issuing a refund or\n  replacement, voiding a sale, charging back a vendor, revoking or\n  terminating a vendor's registration/contract) **OR directly finalizing\n  a counterfeit-authenticity determination** (declaring an item\n  counterfeit, certifying an item as genuine, resolving an authenticity\n  claim) -- the latter is new relative to ISIC 4751/4719 and specific to\n  this vertical's counterfeit-risk exposure (branded apparel/footwear/\n  leather goods).\n- Two ESCALATE (SOFT) gates, either forces human sign-off:\n  `:flag-quality-concern` ALWAYS escalates (never a member of any\n  phase's `:auto` set, at any phase -- two independent layers agree: the\n  governor's own `always-escalate-ops` AND `apparelops.phase`'s own\n  phase table); a `:coordinate-supply-order` above a $1000\n  domain-illustrative cost threshold also always escalates; low\n  confidence also escalates.\n- **This fleet's own known self-tripping bug class** -- a governor\n  scope-exclusion term phrased as a bare noun (e.g. \"refund\", \"dispute\",\n  \"counterfeit\") accidentally matching inside the mock advisor's own\n  legitimate default proposal text and self-blocking the happy path --\n  is avoided from the start: every `scope-excluded-terms` entry in\n  `apparelops.governor` is phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION\n  (\"issue the refund\", \"declare the item counterfeit\", \"certify the item\n  as genuine\"), never a bare noun, in both English and Japanese. A\n  dedicated regression test,\n  `apparelops.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`,\n  asserts all four default proposal generators (including\n  `:flag-quality-concern`, whose own `:op` keyword literally contains\n  the substring \"quality-concern\" and whose default rationale\n  legitimately mentions \"偽造品の疑い\" [suspicion of counterfeit] as a\n  bare descriptive noun, not a finalization action) never trip\n  `:scope-excluded` or `:op-not-allowed`.\n- Staged rollout Phase 0 (read-only) -> Phase 1 (sales-record logging\n  only, approval-gated) -> Phase 2 (+ staffing/supply-order proposals,\n  approval-gated) -> Phase 3 (governor-clean, high-confidence,\n  low-cost proposals auto-commit; quality concerns and high-cost supply\n  orders always escalate regardless of phase).\n- Append-only audit ledger for every log/schedule/order/flag decision\n  (commit, hold, and approval-requested/granted/rejected facts).\n- Fully portable `.cljc` with no JVM-only interop anywhere in `src/`\n  (mock-only advisor; a real LLM would be swapped in behind the same\n  `Advisor` protocol).\n\nFull module set published: `deps.edn`, `blueprint.edn`\n(`:itonami.blueprint/governor :apparel-retail-governor` -- distinct,\nindependently-named from sibling 47xx governors, e.g. ISIC 4751's\n`:textile-retail-governor` and ISIC 4719's `:merchandise-retail-governor`),\n`LICENSE` (AGPL-3.0-or-later), `README.edn`, `GOVERNANCE.md`,\n`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md`,\n`docs/business-model.md`, `docs/operator-guide.md`,\n`src/apparelops/{store,advisor,governor,phase,operation,sim}.cljc`,\n`test/apparelops/{advisor_test,governor_test,governor_contract_test,\nphase_test,store_contract_test}.clj`.\n\n58 tests / 170 assertions green (`clojure -M:test`), independently\nre-verified against a fresh clone of `origin/main`\n(`b38284aa22e37200fbb20c579d56ab08fa5c312d`) after push; clj-kondo\n`--fail-level error` 0 errors / 0 warnings; `clojure -M:run` demo driver\nexercises the full happy path (phase-1 approval-gated commit, phase-3\nauto-commits, a high-cost supply-order escalation, a quality-concern\nescalation) plus all 5 HARD-hold scenarios (unregistered store,\nregistered-but-unverified store, unverified supply-order vendor, a\ndirect-actuation `:effect :commit` attempt, and a proposal drifted into\nthe permanently-excluded quality-dispute/counterfeit-determination\nscope) end-to-end against the real langgraph-clj StateGraph, not a stub.\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry`'s `registry.edn` `\"4771\"` entry is promoted from\n`:spec` to `:implemented`: `:name` de-truncated to the full ISIC class\nname, `:repo`/`:business-id` de-placeholdered from\n`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-G4771` -> `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4771`\n/ `cloud-itonami-isic-4771`, `:operating-states` updated to\n`[:intake :advise :govern :approve :commit :audit]` to match the actor\nstate machine (mirroring ISIC 4719's own operating-states convention for\nan approval-gated coordination actor); `:required-technologies`/\n`:optional-technologies` left unchanged (already correct in the\npre-existing entry). The separate `{:id \"477\" ...}` 3-digit group entry\nis left untouched.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- An independent clothing/footwear/leather specialized-store operator\n  gets an auditable, forkable operations-coordination platform instead\n  of surrendering sales/staffing/supply-order/quality-concern data to a\n  closed back-office SaaS.\n- The actor structurally cannot finalize a refund/replacement/chargeback/\n  vendor-registration-revocation OR a counterfeit-authenticity\n  determination on its own initiative -- those remain human-owned\n  decisions, permanently, not a rollout milestone still to come.\n- `kotoba.industry/maturity-summary`'s fleet-wide `:implemented` count\n  advances by one from this promotion (recomputed live via\n  `(kotoba.industry/maturity-summary)` against a freshly re-fetched\n  `origin/main` `registry.edn` immediately before the `industry_test.clj`\n  edit, not assumed -- see that test file's own dedicated\n  `cloud-itonami-isic-4771-is-implemented` regression entry for the\n  exact before/after count).\n- Extending coverage (e.g. a return-authorization-intake op or a\n  shrinkage-observation check) is additive: add the op to the closed\n  allowlist with its own HARD checks and tests, following the same\n  independent-governor-re-verifies-against-the-actor's-own-records\n  pattern this repo's four flagship checks already establish.\n\n## References\n\n- Repository: https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4771\n  (commit `b38284aa22e37200fbb20c579d56ab08fa5c312d` on `main`)\n- Reference mirror: https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4751\n- Wave 2 plan: ADR-2607121000\n  (`90-docs/adr/2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan.edn`)\n- Sibling de-truncation precedent: ADR-2695004753 (ISIC 4753)\n- Registry: `kotoba-lang/industry`, `resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn`\n  `\"4771\"` entry; test corroboration in `test/kotoba/industry_test.clj`", :adr/decision "{:escalate-always [:flag-quality-concern], :escalate-threshold {:op :coordinate-supply-order, :estimated-cost-usd 1000}, :license \"AGPL-3.0-or-later\", :advisor \"ApparelRetailAdvisor\", :modules [\"deps.edn\" \"blueprint.edn\" \"LICENSE\" \"README.edn\" \"GOVERNANCE.md\" \"CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\" \"CONTRIBUTING.md\" \"SECURITY.md\" \"docs/business-model.md\" \"docs/operator-guide.md\" \"src/apparelops/store.cljc\" \"src/apparelops/advisor.cljc\" \"src/apparelops/governor.cljc\" \"src/apparelops/phase.cljc\" \"src/apparelops/operation.cljc\" \"src/apparelops/sim.cljc\" \"test/apparelops/advisor_test.clj\" \"test/apparelops/governor_test.clj\" \"test/apparelops/governor_contract_test.clj\" \"test/apparelops/phase_test.clj\" \"test/apparelops/store_contract_test.clj\"], :allowed-ops [:log-sales-record :schedule-staffing-operation :coordinate-supply-order :flag-quality-concern], :self-trip-regression-test \"apparelops.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion\", :portable-cljc? true, :governor \"ApparelRetailGovernor\", :governor-keyword :apparel-retail-governor, :phases {0 :read-only, 1 :assisted-logging, 2 :assisted-coordination, 3 :supervised-auto}, :mirrors \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4751\", :jvm-only-interop? false, :effect-invariant :propose, :repo \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4771\", :hard-checks [:store-unverified :vendor-unverified :effect-not-propose :scope-exclusion-folds-op-not-allowed], :namespace \"apparelops\", :scope-exclusion-covers [:quality-dispute-resolution-finalization :counterfeit-authenticity-determination-finalization], :scope-exclusion-new-vs-4751 [:counterfeit-authenticity-determination-finalization]}", :adr/date "2026-07-16", :db/id -1, :adr/wave-ref "ADR-2607121000", :adr/verification "{:demo-command \"clojure -M:run\", :lint-command \"clojure -M:lint\", :demo-covers [:phase-1-approval-gated-commit :phase-3-auto-commit :high-cost-supply-order-escalation :quality-concern-escalation :unregistered-store-hard-hold :unverified-store-hard-hold :unverified-vendor-hard-hold :non-propose-effect-hard-hold :scope-excluded-content-hard-hold], :test-command \"clojure -M:test\", :test-result {:tests 58, :assertions 170, :failures 0, :errors 0}, :lint-result {:errors 0, :warnings 0}, :re-verified-against-fresh-clone? true, :commit-sha \"b38284aa22e37200fbb20c579d56ab08fa5c312d\", :branch \"main\"}", :adr/title "cloud-itonami ISIC 4771 clothing/footwear/leather retail coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references "{:repo-url \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4771\", :reference-mirror-url \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4751\", :wave-plan-adr \"2607121000\", :truncation-precedent-adr \"2695004753\", :registry-file \"resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn\", :registry-repo \"kotoba-lang/industry\", :registry-test-file \"test/kotoba/industry_test.clj\"}"}]